# LPE Fleet Audit - hosts file
# ============================
# Format (one host per line):
#   user@host           - explicit user
#   host                - uses default user (-u flag or current $USER)
#   host:port           - non-standard SSH port
#   user@host:port      - both
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Examples (uncomment and edit for your fleet):

# admin@web-01.example.com
# admin@web-02.example.com
# admin@db-01.example.com:2222
# root@bastion.example.com
# 10.0.1.50
# 10.0.1.51
# 10.0.1.52

# For Kubernetes nodes with shared key:
#   ./fleet-audit.sh -i hosts.txt -u ubuntu -k ~/.ssh/cluster_key.pem --sudo

# For mixed environment:
#   ./fleet-audit.sh -i hosts.txt -c 16 --sudo
